,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c70ed33bfd60535d27e7c4e6969e231d2624324d10654a64db1183f304d47f82.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121250/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "798800a5-255a-5738-91d2-21c2a78e4fb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121250"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection/933b787c39ce6154b96b98235228b42da268d68484311913ea84dd1872295a50" :answer/id #uuid "955a45c2-3d44-50a9-9749-2b706961c601" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/37000a15f2b6164932675c0f0e6dd78fa0ef3015dcc25b27d7dce139e8a1ce4b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection/ae1d83b1d213159187c9fd51ae8571b7f28d618fbd1d451d677c2c0f7d51f5da" :answer/id #uuid "75e0d189-83aa-5e91-ba78-350f1be157b4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/e019652dcfef9bb06dcecb42c1544e93b2f2909cfc1a40aac1eee3cf24f73e7e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection/09558ed973552be5d15c9c0dc4695fa6829ea190fda18428a44419de2ba005a5" :answer/id #uuid "3cbe9a2b-995d-55f2-b24d-503f29268df3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/6cd862eaf47308e250abc6cd4016bcb84132de849b289753751840f9c44c107f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection/8ba16535a595a1802a77df3f8b9b7078a52afbd8813386942fd1b40f01a78d28" :answer/id #uuid "bce225d5-b984-589e-9aca-90205962bcf6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/596e25c1d1f8a0e738d8853c17c77c2f6174a2c314a94ce1674f37b3a4c5c72b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection/2d0581ea5bb8dd99da282f8d5d3b873f795b0970ae0acf5256b67018e1c4512f" :answer/id #uuid "35431708-0a8d-5b0a-9741-95a024239061" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/03b7fe2ba61cbe2608c37a78c82001f6a1fdebdb59f0be0785d55ee119ba8ff4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7280ff46-59be-55c7-973e-e407342d2906" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121260/selection/8ba16535a595a1802a77df3f8b9b7078a52afbd8813386942fd1b40f01a78d28" :answer-field/choices ["q-121260/selection/933b787c39ce6154b96b98235228b42da268d68484311913ea84dd1872295a50" "q-121260/selection/ae1d83b1d213159187c9fd51ae8571b7f28d618fbd1d451d677c2c0f7d51f5da" "q-121260/selection/09558ed973552be5d15c9c0dc4695fa6829ea190fda18428a44419de2ba005a5" "q-121260/selection/8ba16535a595a1802a77df3f8b9b7078a52afbd8813386942fd1b40f01a78d28" "q-121260/selection/2d0581ea5bb8dd99da282f8d5d3b873f795b0970ae0acf5256b67018e1c4512f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121260" :question/id #uuid "d5c43f92-1d47-5cfd-b20e-cd7a27e69c8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-121260" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-7xy.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c44c38febc908fe5e941978bf44bab2e2cb4bd250765950d84f9294c9c4c9c4b.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/209576cd78e9beb1c0f7a9bce8267163df1668a830ffc5c06918f8a726600fbe.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-7x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/cf7fdbafdf968d3e6adfe9544a3b9e5e1736ce22fc808567f1d66fc80916534e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121261/selection/8ba16535a595a1802a77df3f8b9b7078a52afbd8813386942fd1b40f01a78d28" :answer/id #uuid "a33f2308-0495-5d88-b275-f9452aeba209" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/596e25c1d1f8a0e738d8853c17c77c2f6174a2c314a94ce1674f37b3a4c5c72b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121261/selection/1f7378349c6cf507735c773ab7331cb895375a5c98a820bf2ac3c9cb5a0cf4cc" :answer/id #uuid "53d7a4e9-1e5b-597b-ab95-e92a10d43c43" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r