o the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{3}$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/1dd5d0fd4074cbd3a82a2979d2a46d7f5ff02c5411e39ea25b5fae6a0e7e7b56.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9419"] :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y) = -3xy^2.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y > 0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y <                0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<         0$ | $x> 0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y^2$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/743df5f5c9232346866a01aed9afa3d41fff0f61bf7812b7ae5db9a43efe59f4.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y > 0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y <                0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n|  | $x<         0$ | $x> 0$ |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9423"] :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y) = -6x^2y.$ Determine the region that gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y) \\geq 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-6x^2$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/17dd9e10234b6a69123241a882e267d95d505d1944d7c31ef563f9ac06b990af.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
